+"""Aggregate fail-closed proof replay of the dart package (adversarial review round 2, SERIOUS 2, 5, 7).
+Usage: replay_all.py --pin PINFILE [--shards N] [--mode proof|quick] [--certs DIR] [--run-id ID]
+  --shards N   a canonical integer 1 <= N <= 64 (default 7): exactly N replay processes per log, each must succeed
+  --mode       'proof' (default): every certificate recomputed; the only mode that can print PASS.
+               'quick': structure only (no recomputation); it can never print PASS (it prints STRUCTURE-ONLY, NOT A PROOF).
+               'test' : machinery test on a subset (--only TAG,..., --gates all|none); it can never print PASS.
+  --pin        the reviewed file list ('sha256  path' lines): every listed file must have exactly that sha256, at the start and
+               at the end, and every transitive decision source of every stage must be listed (no unpinned code).
+Nothing is reused: every replay runs fresh into replays/run_<ID>/ (an existing run directory or receipt is never overwritten).
+Receipt replays/receipts/<ID>.jsonl: append-only (created with O_EXCL), hash-chained records (each carries the sha256 of the
+previous record), fsynced, binding: the pin list and its verification, the driver and wrapper sources, the runtime identity
+(binding.runtime_identity) and floating-point environment, every gate (command, exit status, output sha256), every merge
+(output sha256), every replay (log and manifest sha256, family, expected binding, every shard output sha256 and summary, the
+strict validation of every receipt record against the recomputed leaf multiset of the log), and the end-of-run checks (pin
